#{[{:activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088758} :activity/id #uuid "fb7a132a-7adf-51d5-b01a-ed19474e4867" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049456 :topic/id #uuid "f6e279fc-81eb-5f98-9ec1-265f25361906" :topic/math-academy-id 848} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088758 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088902 :tutorial/content "The equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $\\color{red}a$ and a vertical radius of length $\\color{blue}b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{x^2}{{\\color{red}a}^2}+\\dfrac{y^2}{{\\color{blue}b}^2}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\n![](images/92/9227839bbf9a01312c3014d336a88176eecd73aa934fcd4741c11271b1e0bea6.png)\n\nTo demonstrate, let's determine the equation of the following ellipse. The horizontal radius has length $\\color{red}a=3$ and the vertical radius has length $\\color{blue}b=2.$\n\n![](images/fe/fe7dff90438e9571ae599a446e355776fbd36ed4746dd76e6633f3848e1f6bbc.png)\n\nTherefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{3}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{2}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "dfd31765-db4b-5a8f-a4f9-3cd31b487aea" :tutorial/math-academy-id 3347 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "36e8b9ee-bc84-580d-871e-f8f79a6f06fa" :step/math-academy-id 464704 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088759}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088759 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087839 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087515 :question/id #uuid "446ea007-1ff4-5023-8e3f-7f00eb0fb2d0" :question/math-academy-id "e-5071"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f88c1deb-cd11-5b68-b90b-2d8edfae2469" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048432} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048811}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088323} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088324} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295041} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295042} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295043} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295044} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186336013} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342034} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186369182} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186369999} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186370002} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186370993}] :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Equation of a Wide Ellipse"} :step/id #uuid "170ade24-159a-5d44-8c0e-76b19230035f" :step/math-academy-id 464705 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088760}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088760 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087840 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087516 :question/id #uuid "af56117c-65e0-5f12-9780-7a95e6be829e" :question/math-academy-id "e-5072"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "de557d1d-5f27-50e3-bcba-22b21f83267f" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088122} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088325} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250346} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250347} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250348} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250349} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284499} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186294935} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295045} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295046} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186336014} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186336015} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342039} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345158} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345178} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186370005} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186370008} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186370011} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186370014} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186370017} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421556} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434278}] :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Equation of a Tall Ellipse"} :step/id #uuid "4f0c0c1a-1d65-50f3-8ad6-64c8261515cf" :step/math-academy-id 464708 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088761}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088761 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088903 :tutorial/content "The **axes** of an ellipse are the horizontal and vertical diameters of the ellipse.\n\n- The **major axis** of an ellipse is the *larger* of the horizontal and vertical diameters.\n\n- The **minor axis** of an ellipse is the *shorter* of the horizontal and vertical diameters.\n\nFor example, the ellipse below has a major axis of $6$ and a minor axis of $4.$\n\n![](images/42/426ef9412a96730e50d78437fce2f1d45d7be4d4c175e3a230f4a696e0811189.png)\n\nThe **semi-axes** of an ellipse are the horizontal and vertical radii of the ellipse.\n\n- The **semi-major axis** of an ellipse is the *larger* of the horizontal and vertical radii. In other words, it is half the length of the major axis.\n\n- The **semi-minor axis** of an ellipse is the *shorter* of the horizontal and vertical radii. In other words, it is half the length of the minor axis.\n\nFor example, the ellipse below has a semi-major axis of length $3$ and a semi-minor axis of length $2.$\n\n![](images/b0/b031900464b03a9c2c2a7a9fe4cfaf40932f8d0c76b9d952cebf64d82a6261bc.png)" :tutorial/id #uuid "fd403f68-d6b8-5336-b699-87bcfaeadef8" :tutorial/math-academy-id 3348 :tutorial/title "Major and Minor Axes"} :step/id #uuid "bacaca5a-c3a9-5061-9de7-c982a78a225f" :step/math-academy-id 464711 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088762}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088762 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087841 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087517 :question/id #uuid "b7c94673-f847-5977-9b9f-8d235ea42eb2" :question/math-academy-id "e-5073"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4e43e393-8752-58bc-b87c-b72f679cbfd9" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049923}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088321} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088322} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250350} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250351} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284503} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284508} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186294936} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295047} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295048} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295049} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295050} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295051} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295052} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335983} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345141} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345157} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186370020} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186396120} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186396127} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186399850} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186401537} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434277} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434279}] :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Lengths of the Major and Minor Axes Given the Equation of an Ellipse"} :step/id #uuid "c6b41627-794b-5ac3-b0e8-df5ed175150e" :step/math-academy-id 464712}] :activity/title "Equations of Ellipses Centered at the Origin" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186087919}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046658} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421558} :activity/id #uuid "f98781fb-0e3e-56a0-8fd8-a889cb513084" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049456 :topic/id #uuid "f6e279fc-81eb-5f98-9ec1-265f25361906" :topic/math-academy-id 848} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421557 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186399850 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d4ffa0ff-df0b-5bc5-b896-3f6772a35019" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$28$ and $24$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399852} {:answer/id #uuid "e8f1177f-3e11-593f-ad9c-dda3299fba50" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$24.5$ and $18$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399853} {:answer/id #uuid "e59ee665-26a4-5d2e-8c55-26143f2480d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$14$ and $12$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399854} {:answer/id #uuid "ee829b75-97f1-545e-8cf4-3704340f4ba1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$49$ and $36$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399855} {:answer/id #uuid "f8e390e1-9f85-5321-a954-3f147b97e82b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$7$ and $6$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399856}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186399854} :answer-field/id #uuid "44102d96-20a4-51fc-add2-7a7a026df6ba" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399851}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "3113828e-6ca6-530b-804d-2cdc91aade73" :question/math-academy-id "q-115134" :question/problem "What are the lengths of the major and minor axes of an ellipse with equation \n$\\frac{{x}^{2}}{49}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{36}=1?$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have ${a}^{2}=49$ and ${b}^{2}=36.$\n\n- Since ${a}^{2}=49,$ the length of the horizontal radius must be $a=\\sqrt{49}=7.$\n\n- Since ${b}^{2}=36,$ the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{36}=6.$\n\nThus, the semi-major axis has length $a=7,$ and the semi-minor axis has length $b=6.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2a=2\\cdot 7=14,$ and the minor axis has length $2b=2\\cdot 6=12.$"} :step/id #uuid "047f66db-66e3-5f7a-9815-4fd47c15afae" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421559}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421558 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335983 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "447870c5-0e16-591a-8300-97b1a1b53090" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$14$ and $4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333622} {:answer/id #uuid "548b03ca-4238-5b00-9cb4-91def2cc07cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$14\\sqrt{2}$ and $4\\sqrt{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333761} {:answer/id #uuid "68381630-1c58-5c47-b731-887a1f1decb0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$7$ and $4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333945} {:answer/id #uuid "6aa132ec-2b5e-506f-9009-d06c05f62c18" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$7$ and $2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333966} {:answer/id #uuid "f94f55ce-3720-511d-baaa-529e5639ba46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$7\\sqrt{2}$ and $2\\sqrt{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335173}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186333622} :answer-field/id #uuid "c27addb0-e02b-555b-8abb-615b89631ce7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335594}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "50aac069-cc6f-51ae-b729-84e72b0989dd" :question/math-academy-id "q-69563" :question/problem "What are the lengths of the major and minor axes of an ellipse with equation \n$\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{49}=1?$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have ${a}^{2}=4$ and ${b}^{2}=49.$\n\n- Since ${a}^{2}=4,$ the length of the horizontal radius must be $a=\\sqrt{4}=2.$\n\n- Since ${b}^{2}=49,$ the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{49}=7.$\n\nSo the semi-major axis has length $b=7,$ and the semi-minor axis has length $a=2.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2b=2\\cdot 7=14,$ and the minor axis has length $2a=2\\cdot 2=4.$"} :step/id #uuid "05a824a1-fef7-52fd-b42e-f37a8a9561f2" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421560}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421559 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186294935 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "92fade62-72f5-5c55-aa78-c2d0dbaf2b44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{49}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293509}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186293509} :answer-field/id #uuid "a9711613-beb2-54c9-ab19-cae6c7783280" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294539}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "5ee547bf-f7e1-51f3-bed2-e58fc1c418f5" :question/math-academy-id "q-277921" :question/problem "![](images/ab/ab3d1fefcefa12133ec4ea7e3e6ce744c88f5a9b25029c950254706097cb4c4d.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?\n\n{{field-1}}$=1$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the horizontal radius has length $a=2$ and the vertical radius has length $b=7.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{2}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{7}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{49} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "343e00c9-2c9c-5130-85cb-9db7d2b119ce" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421561}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421560 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421556 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3c37fde0-293d-5fff-8b41-8792f1c3b2d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{25}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{49}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421550} {:answer/id #uuid "60162dda-59fc-569f-9bbc-f89a1da9b64e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{16}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{49}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421551} {:answer/id #uuid "650d25a5-3c4b-5948-9c9f-4ca92962040c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{5}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{7}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421552} {:answer/id #uuid "7a4b634a-7190-518b-8a3e-0e64b953f99a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{49}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421553} {:answer/id #uuid "f7ee88ea-070f-5d68-aaa9-8fb89bd88756" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{7}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{5}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421554}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421550} :answer-field/id #uuid "a872ab99-4b04-549f-a3e0-8010a8cc8418" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421555}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "05225557-6476-5115-9d07-1e8467a995db" :question/math-academy-id "q-73631" :question/problem "![](images/39/3989e71a908c5536d97732e253effe16fadb6382a90610db0a8693eec8161393.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the horizontal radius has length $a=5$ and the vertical radius has length $b=7.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{5}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{7}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{25}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{49} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "9002f488-6289-5d99-b35a-dbc5df691ad1" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421557}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421561 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295049 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ee64a24f-4e3c-5796-94b8-769faa4d203e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293859}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186293859} :answer-field/id #uuid "4d433ad7-9ca0-5240-8e86-ff3b484b7323" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294199} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c1efda85-532c-5456-9085-146b731f4efb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293689}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186293689} :answer-field/id #uuid "eb9daf9a-554c-59f2-8703-ec452d9cbcc0" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294757}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "c976c0d3-2975-5e8a-a067-1b42fba6644e" :question/math-academy-id "q-279169" :question/problem "For the ellipse $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25}=1,$ find the lengths of its major and minor axes.\n\n$\\,$ The length of the major axis is \n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The length of the minor axis is \n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have ${a}^{2}=4$ and ${b}^{2}=25.$\n\n- Since ${a}^{2}=4,$ the length of the horizontal radius must be $a=\\sqrt{4}=2.$\n\n- Since ${b}^{2}=25,$ the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{25}=5.$\n\nThus, the semi-major axis has length $b=5,$ and the semi-minor axis has length $a=2.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2b=2\\cdot 5=10,$ and the minor axis has length $2a=2\\cdot 2=4.$"} :step/id #uuid "ba407b04-0f45-5fb8-bef8-bfffcd4599ad"}] :activity/title "Equations of Ellipses Centered at the Origin" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421549}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046658} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434284} :activity/id #uuid "2d86a4f4-b8ba-5875-b01b-334ee3c8800c" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049456 :topic/id #uuid "f6e279fc-81eb-5f98-9ec1-265f25361906" :topic/math-academy-id 848} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434280 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434277 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1dcd62ed-d1d5-5d66-b9a7-d3752b72ffcb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434263}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434263} :answer-field/id #uuid "5f59ee40-6a49-5f76-9b09-b56f1e7b8c65" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434274} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2cb3f03d-cfef-5f9f-b396-26b221d4f856" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434266}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434266} :answer-field/id #uuid "62dc0b83-a470-59d2-b62b-b5ccbaa907c1" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434275}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "3c46acbe-8af8-5805-a582-9ade9300c9a5" :question/math-academy-id "q-279199" :question/problem "For the ellipse $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{13}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{36}=1,$ find the lengths of its major and minor axes.\n\n$\\,$ The length of the major axis is \n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The length of the minor axis is \n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have ${a}^{2}=13$ and ${b}^{2}=36.$\n\n- Since ${a}^{2}=13,$ the length of the horizontal radius must be $a=\\sqrt{13}.$\n\n- Since ${b}^{2}=36,$ the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{36}=6.$\n\nThus, the semi-major axis has length $b=6,$ and the semi-minor axis has length $a=\\sqrt{13}.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2b=2\\cdot 6=12,$ and the minor axis has length $2a=2\\cdot \\sqrt{13}=2\\sqrt{13}.$"} :step/id #uuid "54f488a2-5ee1-5f4b-9b2d-7bfa683c828f"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434281 :step/content {:db/id #